        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): bound AGENTS.md and root-memory file reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`shouldSuggestMemorySystem` and `migrateLegacyRootMemoryFile` in `src/commands/doctor-workspace.ts` read `AGENTS.md`, `MEMORY.md`, and archived `memory.md` with unbounded `fs.promises.readFile(..., \"utf-8\")`. A malicious or runaway workspace file could OOM the doctor repair path before any diagnosis or merge.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- `AGENTS.md` is only scanned for a memory-system reference, so a 1 MiB cap is plenty.\n- Root memory files are markdown journals; 8 MiB is generous while preventing runaway files from OOMing migration.\n- Existing `catch` behavior is preserved: an oversized/unreadable `AGENTS.md` is treated as missing guidance, and an oversized memory pair is archived but not merged.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- `openclaw doctor` workspace memory checks no longer buffer arbitrarily large files.\n- Oversized `AGENTS.md` / memory files are handled gracefully instead of crashing.\n- Normal workspace doctor flows work exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Replaced unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` calls with `readRegularFile` capped reads in `src/commands/doctor-workspace.ts`.\n- Added regression tests in `src/commands/doctor-workspace.test.ts` covering an oversized `AGENTS.md` and an oversized legacy memory file.\n- Local test run:\n  ```\n  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-workspace.test.ts --run\n  # 5 tests passed\n  ```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI created a standalone Node script at `/tmp/proof-101448.mjs` that imports the real helpers from `src/commands/doctor-workspace.ts` and exercises both the normal and oversized paths in isolated temp workspaces:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx /tmp/proof-101448.mjs\n=== OpenClaw PR 101448 real behavior proof ===\n\nNormal AGENTS.md -> shouldSuggestMemorySystem = false\n  (expected false because AGENTS.md references MEMORY.md)\n\nOversized AGENTS.md (2 MiB) -> shouldSuggestMemorySystem = true\n  (expected true: oversized file is treated as missing guidance)\n\nNormal split-brain root memory -> migrateLegacyRootMemoryFile:\n  changed: true\n  mergedLegacy: true\n  archiveOnly: false\n  (expected changed=true, mergedLegacy=true, archiveOnly=false)\n\nOversized legacy memory.md (9 MiB) -> migrateLegacyRootMemoryFile:\n  changed: true\n  mergedLegacy: false\n  archiveOnly: true\n  archivedLegacyPath: /tmp/proof-101448-VTwxDZ/.openclaw-repair/root-memory/2026-07-07T10-29-48-239Z/memory.md\n  (expected changed=true, mergedLegacy=false, archiveOnly=true)\n```\n\nInterpretation:\n\n- Normal inputs continue to work: a workspace with a conventional `AGENTS.md` referencing `MEMORY.md` is recognized as already having memory guidance, and a normal split-brain `MEMORY.md`/`memory.md` pair is merged.\n- Oversized inputs are rejected before any downstream processing: a 2 MiB `AGENTS.md` exceeds the 1 MiB cap and is treated as missing guidance, and a 9 MiB legacy `memory.md` exceeds the 8 MiB cap so the legacy file is archived but its content is not merged into `MEMORY.md` (`archiveOnly: true`).\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-doctor-workspace-memory-reads",
